From 78122652f1258b3900d7fd721c9b1df06d4122d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MT6762 local experiment <mt6762-build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:19:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm: add explicit PMIC gauge snapshot laboratory fixture

AI-assisted local experiment, not intended for upstream submission. Adds synthetic initialized gauge registers, bounded latch snapshots and counter progress with ownership/calibration faults. Rejects destructive writes and does not model SOC, capacity or physical current.
---
 docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst        | 23 +++++++++++
 hw/arm/mt6762.c                   | 28 ++++++++++++-
 hw/arm/mt6762_lab_power.c         | 69 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 include/hw/arm/mt6762_lab_power.h |  7 ++++
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_gauge.py    | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_power.py    |  5 ++-
 6 files changed, 191 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/mt6762/test_lab_gauge.py

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
index 2253e9c..d67b723 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
@@ -246,3 +246,26 @@ ADC isolation and default absence. Native ``--native-lab-thermal`` separately
 asserts ``pmic-thermal-adc-owned``. Host scheduling may let a short conversion
 finish before the guest observes READY-low; conservative guest rejection is
 expected and must not be reported as a valid fresh sample.
+
+Explicit synthetic gauge snapshots
+----------------------------------
+
+``lab-gauge=on`` requires ``lab-power=on`` and independently enables a
+synthetic initialized PMIC gauge. Its calibration registers and100-unit
+raw current are invented fixtures, not observations from this phone. A
+synthetic2Hz NTER counter establishes snapshot progression. No battery SOC,
+capacity, coulomb history, lifetime or physical current source is modeled.
+
+The model implements the bounded latch/read/release sequence and rejects
+reset, calibration, gain and offset writes. ``gauge-timeout``,
+``gauge-latch-stuck``, ``gauge-stale``, ``gauge-clock``, ``gauge-calibration``
+and ``gauge-counter-stuck`` extend ``lab-power-fault``. Read-only state exposes
+snapshot/command counts, control and counter values. The native driver must
+reject the first baseline snapshot as a fresh current observation and wait
+for counter progression before publishing current validity.
+
+``tests/mt6762/test_lab_gauge.py`` independently exercises exact latch
+commands, progression, all faults, rejected destructive writes and default
+absence. The XNU loader's ``--native-lab-gauge`` asserts only the matching
+synthetic calibration/ownership contract. These values must never be copied
+into a physical-phone handoff without independent live validation.
diff --git a/hw/arm/mt6762.c b/hw/arm/mt6762.c
index ce30054..9ae7878 100644
